                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "238539852",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561199498782392",
                            "num_reviews": 14,
                            "playtime_forever": 455,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 455,
                            "last_played": 1792924726
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Being part of Digital Eclipse's early works in game preservation, The Disney Afternoon Collection becomes a love letter of the iconic Capcom x Disney collaboration on making classic games.\r\n\r\nSome issues to point out is the absence of cheats like infinite lives and invincibility compared to Digital Eclipse's modern works like Rayman: 30th Anniversary Edition and Toy Story: Retro Roundup. Also, I noticed in a few games, the frames of the old Eclipse Engine (yes, not the current Bakesale Engine) can drop for a few seconds, sometimes feeling like a commerical-free NES emulator.\r\n\r\nDespite these minor issues, it's still a fun way to access these games that were way difficult back in the day.\r\n\r\nNow, gimme a sequel but this time all about Mickey Mouse and I'll be satisfied and buy it day one.",
